{"title":"1953 AHSME Problems/Problem 40","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems/Problem_40&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The negation of the statement \"all men are honest,\" is:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/f/62faa3f5dbc9c479c1e9bb8e0b246a771d6464a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\text{no men are honest} \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ \\text{all men are dishonest} \\\\  \\textbf{(C)}\\ \\text{some men are dishonest}\\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ \\text{no men are dishonest}\\\\ \\textbf{(E)}\\ \\text{some men are honest}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"428\" height=\"57\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems/Problem_40&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A statement and its negation cannot both be true or both be false at the same time.  Only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6ef7ec511bb37f9686b9c308d8eb7d5ae57444b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\text{some men are dishonest}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"220\" height=\"30\" /> qualifies as such.\n</p><p>Choice A is incorrect, as if some but not all men are honest, both this statement and the original statement are false.\n</p><p>Choice B is incorrect, as if some but not all men are honest, both this statement and the original statement are false.\n</p><p>Choice D is incorrect, as it is logically equivalent to the original statement.  That is, this statement and the original statement must be either both false or both true.\n</p><p>Choice E is incorrect, as if no men are honest, both this and the original statement are false.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems/Problem_40&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME\" title=\"1953 AHSME\">1953 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1953 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1953 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1953\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems/Problem_39\" title=\"1953 AHSME Problems/Problem 39\">Problem 39</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems/Problem_41\" title=\"1953 AHSME Problems/Problem 41\">Problem 41</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1953 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1953 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1953 AHSME Pro